sequenceDiagram

actor Caller as Customer or administrator
participant Server as server.js
participant Route as routes/bookings.js + guards + validation
participant C as controllers/bookings.js
participant S as services/bookings.js
participant M as Provider / User / Vehicle / ProviderApplication / Booking
participant DB as MongoDB
Caller->>Server: POST /api/v1/bookings or PATCH /bookings/{bookingId}
Server->>Route: Parsed JSON
Route->>Route: Authenticate, POST customer only, PATCH customer/admin, validate
Route->>C: req.actor + req.validated
C->>S: createBooking or updateBookingDates
activate S
S->>M: Read vehicle provider or ownership-scoped booking references
M->>DB: Preliminary references
S->>DB: Start snapshot transaction
S->>M: Increment Provider revision
M->>DB: Provider guard
S->>M: Increment User bookingRevision
M->>DB: Customer cap guard
S->>M: Increment owned Vehicle revision
M->>DB: Vehicle guard
opt Date edit
    S->>M: Re-read ownership-scoped booking in session
    Note over S,M: Require not cancelled and today before original start
end
S->>S: Validate Thailand dates and 1–30 inclusive rental days
S->>M: Check approved provider/profile, active vehicle and offering period
M->>DB: Eligibility reads in same session
S->>M: Count customer non-completed bookings, check vehicle overlap
M->>DB: Exclude current booking ID on edits
Note over S,M: Reject cap of three or inclusive overlap with 409
alt Create
    S->>S: Snapshot vehicle and current rate, calculate satang total
else Edit
    S->>S: Retain snapshot/rate, recalculate days and total
end
S->>M: Save booking in session
M->>DB: Persist booking
DB-->>S: Commit
S->>M: Detach session, populate selected current customer contact
M->>DB: Read customer contact after commit
S-->>C: Booking with current customer
deactivate S
C->>C: Serialize with captured Thailand today
C-->>Server: 201 create or 200 edit
Server-->>Caller: JSON response
Note over S,DB: Domain failures abort, eligible transient transaction failures map to safe 409
